  "implementation": [
    "Capture initial reserve/release/exact-token inspection methods before callbacks; register each attempted reservation before invoking it. Throws and explicit refusals cannot orphan a side effect.",
    "Require synchronous initial acknowledgment. A Promise is refused before prepareInput or Worker construction; track its settlement and roll back any late side effect before reporting released.",
    "Keep the shared accounting guard until external reservation retirement is acknowledged. Return a bounded failed-admission diagnostic, a completion receipt and explicit private/batch retry; disposal joins pending retirement instead of admitting a producer.",
    "A false release is accepted only when captured exact-token inspection proves absence. Opaque false remains unknown; successful retries cannot erase live reservations.",
    "The resource budget exposes one immutable O(1) observation for the requested token/owner, without listing or mutating other reservations. Failed-admission records are bounded by maxQueuedJobs+maxWorkers.",
    "Retain every declared worker/caller anchor. Closing that declared graph adds the new owner plus three existing transitive sources; no prior308files are removed. This312file inventory is distinct from the smaller actual cold-worker request observations."
  ],
